From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: unom <packages@unom.io>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 12:57:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 52/52] punktfunk: stamp pfhdr42

A banner shows whether the layer beside it corrects Proton's fullscreen
hack for a game that does not draw BGRA8.
---
 src/meson.build | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/meson.build b/src/meson.build
index 0f32a1d..c423208 100644
--- a/src/meson.build
+++ b/src/meson.build
@@ -234,7 +234,8 @@ vcs_tag = run_command(vcs_tag_cmd, check: false).stdout().strip()
 #   +pfhdr39 — …and a planar capture's chroma starts on a 16-row boundary on Intel
 #   +pfhdr40 — …and a planar capture dmabuf takes a tiled modifier its consumer accepts, on Intel
 #   +pfhdr41 — …and an HDR P010 capture writes full range when its consumer names it
-version_tag = vcs_tag + '+pfhdr41' + ' (' + compiler_name + ' ' + compiler_version + ')'
+#   +pfhdr42 — …and the WSI layer corrects Proton's fullscreen hack for a game that is not BGRA8
+version_tag = vcs_tag + '+pfhdr42' + ' (' + compiler_name + ' ' + compiler_version + ')'
 
 gamescope_version_conf = configuration_data()
 gamescope_version_conf.set('VCS_TAG', version_tag)
